{
  "conceptual": "\n<p sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"3\">Render pipeline passes and extractors often expose properties that affect how a scene is rendered, for example the tonemapping curve or the strength of an effect. These values are normally fixed on the <a href=\"~/pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-overview.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"3\">render pipeline</a> asset, but they can also be <em sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"3\">driven dynamically</em> at runtime, without any C++ or script code, using <a href=\"~/pages/docs/misc/blackboards.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"3\">blackboards</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blackboard-driven-properties\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"5\">Blackboard-Driven Properties</h2>\n<p sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"7\">An <code sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"7\">ezView</code> looks for blackboard entries whose key is structured as <code sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"7\">&lt;PassName&gt;.&lt;PropertyName&gt;</code> or <code sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"7\">&lt;ExtractorName&gt;.&lt;PropertyName&gt;</code>. Whenever such an entry exists, and its name matches a render pass or extractor of the view's active render pipeline as well as one of its member properties, that property is overwritten with the entry's value every frame.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"9\">Two blackboards are checked, in this order of priority:</p>\n<ol sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"11\">\n<li sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"11\"><strong sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"11\">World Blackboard:</strong> Every <a href=\"~/pages/docs/misc/blackboards.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"11\">world</a> has its own blackboard. Use this for values that should apply to every camera looking at that world, for example a global fog setting.</li>\n<li sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"12\"><strong sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"12\">View Blackboard:</strong> An optional, camera-specific blackboard, configured through the <code sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"12\">BlackboardName</code> property on the <a href=\"~/pages/docs/graphics/camera-component.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"12\">camera component</a>. Entries here take priority over entries with the same key from the world blackboard. This is useful for camera-specific overrides, for instance on a <a href=\"~/pages/docs/graphics/render-to-texture/render-to-texture.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"12\">render to texture (TODO)</a> camera that should not be affected by the world's blackboard.</li>\n</ol>\n<p sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"14\">To find out which <code sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"14\">&lt;PassName&gt;.&lt;PropertyName&gt;</code> keys are available, inspect the render passes and extractors of the <a href=\"~/pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-overview.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"14\">render pipeline</a> that is in use.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"16\">Pass and extractor names may contain dots themselves. For a key such as <code sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"16\">Rendering.Pipeline.SSAO.MaxScreenSpaceRadius</code>, every split at a dot is tried, starting with the shortest name, until a pass or extractor with that name is found. The rest of the key is used as the property name.</p>\n<h2 id=\"switches\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"18\">Switches</h2>\n<p sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"20\"><a href=\"~/pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-passes.md#switch-pass\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"20\">Switch passes</a> read their selected value from the same two blackboards, using the entry named in their <code sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"20\">BlackboardProperty</code>. The view blackboard has priority over the world blackboard here as well. Changing the value of such an entry rebuilds the pipeline's pass graph.</p>\n<h2 id=\"pipeline-cvars\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"22\">Pipeline CVars</h2>\n<p sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"24\">All <a href=\"~/pages/docs/debugging/cvars.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"24\">CVars</a> whose name starts with <code sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"24\">Rendering.Pipeline.</code> are automatically copied into the world blackboard, using the full CVar name as the key. Whenever such a CVar changes, the blackboard entry is updated.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"26\">Therefore a pipeline CVar can be used to switch a pipeline feature on or off, or set a property, when a pass or extractor is named like the CVar prefix. This allows exposing graphics settings, without writing code to forward them to the render pipeline. To add a new setting, declare a CVar named <code sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"26\">Rendering.Pipeline.&lt;Something&gt;</code> and reference it in the render pipeline asset.</p>\n<h2 id=\"populating-the-blackboard\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"28\">Populating the Blackboard</h2>\n<p sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"30\">Rather than writing to the blackboard from code, the recommended approach is to use a <a href=\"~/pages/docs/gameplay/volume-sampler-component.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"30\">Volume Sampler Component</a> with its <code sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"30\">WriteToBlackboard</code> property enabled. It samples values out of <a href=\"~/pages/docs/effects/post-processing/volume-components.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"30\">volume components</a> at the camera's position and writes them into the target blackboard using the matching keys, so that render pipeline properties (such as color grading or exposure) change smoothly depending on which area of a level the camera is in.</p>\n<h2 id=\"see-also\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"32\">See Also</h2>\n<ul sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"34\">\n<li sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"34\"><a href=\"~/pages/docs/effects/post-processing/volume-components.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"34\">Volume Components</a></li>\n<li sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"35\"><a href=\"~/pages/docs/gameplay/volume-sampler-component.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"35\">Volume Sampler Component</a></li>\n<li sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"36\"><a href=\"~/pages/docs/misc/blackboards.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"36\">Blackboards</a></li>\n<li sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"37\"><a href=\"~/pages/docs/graphics/camera-component.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"37\">Camera Component</a></li>\n<li sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"38\"><a href=\"~/pages/docs/debugging/cvars.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"38\">CVars</a></li>\n<li sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"39\"><a href=\"~/pages/docs/effects/fog.md\" sourcefile=\"pages/docs/graphics/render-pipeline/render-pipeline-properties.md\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"39\">Fog</a></li>\n</ul>\n",
  "type": "Conceptual",
